We know that the activity of radioactive substance, $A=A_0 e^{-\lambda t}$
\begin{aligned}
& \Rightarrow \quad \frac{A}{A_0}=e^{-\lambda t}=e^{-\frac{0.693}{T^{1 / 2} t}} \quad\left[\because T_{1 / 2}=\frac{0.693}{\lambda}\right] \\
& \Rightarrow \quad \frac{1}{16}=e^{-\frac{0.693 \times 40}{T^{1 / 2}}} \Rightarrow \frac{0.693 \times 40}{T_{1 / 2}}=\ln 16 \\
& \Rightarrow \quad T_{1 / 2}=\frac{0.693 \times 40}{\ln 16}=9.997 \approx 10 \text { days. }
\end{aligned}

