Disodium salt of ethylene diamine tetracetic acid has been used for the estimation of $M^{2+}$ metal ions like $\mathrm{Mg}^{2+}, \mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ etc. by complexometric titrations. In this titration, indicator ions ( $D^{3-}$ ions) form redmetal indicator complex, $\left[M D^{-}\right]$with $M^{2+}$ ions.

\begin{array}{ccc}
\text { (i) } M^{2+}+ & D^{3-} \rightleftharpoons \mathrm{pH}=10 & {\left[M^{2+} D\right]^{-}} \\
\text {metal ion } & \text { indicator } & \text { Metal indicator } \\
\left(\mathrm{Mg}^{2+} \text { or } \mathrm{Ca}^{2+}\right) & \text { ion (blue) } & \text { complex (red) } \\
\text { (ii) }\left[M^{2+} D\right]^{-}+ & \mathrm{EDTA}^{4-} & \rightleftharpoons\left[M^{2+}(\mathrm{EDTA})\right]^{2-}+D^{3-} \\
\text { (red) } & \text { EDTA ion } & \text { metal-EDTA } \\
& & \text { complex }
\end{array}

The release of the free indicator ion is marked by a change from red (colour of $\left[M^{2+} D\right]^{-}$complex) to blue (colour of $D^{3-}$ ion) colour.

